rev:release rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Review v0.2.8" ;
    rdfs:comment "The visual tests of v0.2.8, in the order a person would review them. 1 of this release's 36 parts have a TestWorkflow (6 steps, each a screenshot and what the test checks); 35 do not yet, and are listed under \"No visual test yet\" so the gap stays visible. Select a step, look at its picture, and set pass, fail or a note in the node panel. Generated from the roadmap and the Testing graph by scripts/offline/release-review-space.ts; edit those, not this file. Release status when generated: functional." ;
    hnav:order "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    p:has rev:wf-generated-assets, rev:gap .

rev:wf-generated-assets rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "1. Make pictures, clips and 3D splats on your own machine, and see them in a space" ;
    rdfs:comment "Part of v0.2.8: F58.9.2 F58.9.2 — a node can carry a Gaussian splat, seen in the 3D graph and in the asset viewer (status: functional). Write a prompt, and three local models turn it into a picture, then a short clip and a Gaussian splat (a 3D object drawn as many small soft blobs of color) made from that picture. You can turn a splat and look at it from any side. The results open as their own space, where each one sits on its own node, linked to what it was made from, and one splat can become the background of the space. Run by tests/e2e/workflow-generated-assets.test.ts." ;
    hnav:order "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:gap ;
    p:has rev:wf-generated-assets-01-open-example, rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline, rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture, rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video, rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat, rev:wf-generated-assets-06-background .

rev:wf-generated-assets-01-open-example rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "1. Open the Generated assets example as its own space" ;
    rdfs:comment "Under example data on the About page (or from the welcome page), choose Generated assets. It opens as a new space of its own and shows its graph, so trying it never mixes into the space you were working in. Opening it again refreshes that same space rather than making a second one.\n\nWhere: the About page (/about).\n\nThe test checks: The card offers to open the example as a space; choosing it lands on the graph of the new space, and the Spaces tab then shows Generated assets as the current space." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/01-open-example.webp" ;
    hnav:order "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "2. See the pipeline in the graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "Each result is a node, linked to what it was made from: a prompt to its picture, and the picture to its clip and its splat. Each node lists what its receipt recorded (the model, the seed, how long it took and when) under metadata in its details, not as extra nodes, and its license is a node of its own (MIT or Apache-2.0) that it links to. Turn on preview all to see every result on its node. A node with a splat is drawn inside its splat, which turns slowly.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: With previews on, at least three results show on their nodes (which ones are in view depends on where the layout puts them), and the 3D graph reports both node splats loaded and none failed." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/02-see-pipeline.webp" ;
    hnav:order "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-01-open-example ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "3. The picture, made from a prompt" ;
    rdfs:comment "Z-Image-Turbo, run by stable-diffusion.cpp, turned the prompt into a 768×768 picture in eight steps. Find the picture's node (searching for its name works when it is out of view) and choose its preview to see it large. This picture is the starting point for the next two steps.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The picture the app shows is byte for byte the file its receipt describes (same SHA-256), its check accepted it, its models are MIT or Apache-2.0 licensed, and it opens large at 768 pixels wide." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/03-picture.webp" ;
    hnav:order "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-02-see-pipeline ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "4. The clip, made from the picture" ;
    rdfs:comment "Wan2.2 TI2V-5B, also run by stable-diffusion.cpp, started from the picture and a second prompt describing the motion, and made a 49-frame clip. The check measures how much the last frame differs from the first, because a video model can return a clip in which almost nothing moves. When that happens the receipt says so rather than calling the clip fine.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The clip the app shows matches its receipt, its check accepted it, and it loads in the viewer at 512 pixels wide. The screenshot shows a frame from the middle of the clip." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/04-video.webp" ;
    hnav:order "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-03-picture ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "5. The splat, made from the picture" ;
    rdfs:comment "TripoSplat turned the same picture into 32,768 Gaussians, writing a PLY file of about 2 MB. The first prompt asked for a flat carving seen from above, and TripoSplat made it as flat as a coin; asking for a three-quarter view with a domed shell gave it real depth. Choose the splat on its node to turn it and look at it from any side. Everything it shows on the far side of the turtle was guessed from one picture.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The splat the app shows matches its receipt and its check accepted it, and the viewer reports that it has loaded. The renderer is Gaussian-Splat-Lite, which the app loads only when a splat is on screen." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/05-splat.webp" ;
    hnav:order "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:next rev:wf-generated-assets-06-background ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-04-video ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

rev:wf-generated-assets-06-background rdf:type ktype:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "6. Set a splat as the background of the space" ;
    rdfs:comment "Open the lighthouse island splat and choose Set as background. The island is then drawn large behind the graph, sized to the graph and turning very slowly, and it never gets in the way of choosing a node. The choice is saved with the space, so it travels with an export. Clear background removes it.\n\nWhere: the graph (/).\n\nThe test checks: The island splat matches its receipt. After Set as background the same control offers Clear background, which shows the setting was saved to the space, and the 3D graph reports three splats loaded and none failed: the two on their nodes and the island. Where the island sits and how it looks is shown by the screenshot, not measured by the test." ;
    p:photo "/workflows/generated-assets/06-background.webp" ;
    hnav:order "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:layer "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    hnav:prev rev:wf-generated-assets-05-splat ;
    kmeta:review-verdict "unreviewed" .

